          "title": "You'll want to know: തലച്ചോറ്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തലച്ചോറ് — talaccōṟŭ — \"the brain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തലച്ചോറിന് നല്ല ഉറക്കം ആവശ്യമാണ്. talaccōṟinŭ nalla uṟakkaṁ āvaśyamāṇŭ. The brain needs good sleep."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തല head + ചോറ് cooked rice: the soft matter inside the head."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തലച്ചോറ് (talaccōṟŭ) is native Dravidian, a compound of തല, \"head\" (DEDR 3103), and ചോറ്, which DEDR gives as boiled rice and also brain or marrow (DEDR 2897)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
